% ADJ52 case-20 program (this patient's observations + queries only; no rules).
% 29-year-old man referred to a behavioral-health clinic by his employer for adult
% ADHD assessment. Over ~3 years: progressive forgetfulness/disorganization (losing
% keys and documents, lapses in judgment jeopardizing his job) on a LIFELONG
% scattered/inattentive baseline that had not been disabling until recently. Past
% hyperthyroidism on a daily antithyroid tablet. Years of intermittent low energy,
% itchy skin, restlessness, and longstanding intermittent loose stools. Full-scale
% IQ ~67 (borderline-to-mild); positive items on a standardized adult inattention
% self-report screen; MMSE 27 (near-normal), later falling to the low 20s.
% Exam: generalized hyperreflexia, BILATERAL extensor plantar responses, mild gait
% unsteadiness; later a stiff/dragging spastic gait with bilateral leg tremor. EEG
% non-epileptiform; nerve conduction normal. Thyroid antibody panel: elevated
% antithyroid / antimicrosomal / antithyroglobulin titres -> an autoimmune thyroid
% encephalopathy was considered and high-dose corticosteroid PULSE therapy given:
% NO benefit, then worsening over months. Then noted: firm painless BILATERAL
% ACHILLES TENDON swellings, BILATERAL early CATARACTS, reduced bone mineral density.
% MRI: symmetric T2/FLAIR high signal in the cerebellar white matter and DENTATE
% NUCLEI, cerebral peduncles, posterior limbs of internal capsules, and hypothalamus.
% CSF unremarkable for infection/inflammation/malignancy.

% --- the correlated multisystem xanthomatosis signature (one mechanism; fires once) ---
observe exam_finding(bilateral_achilles_tendon_swellings)
observe exam_finding(bilateral_early_cataracts)
observe symptom(chronic_intermittent_diarrhea)
observe test_result(reduced_bone_mineral_density)

% --- the specific dentate-centered MRI signature ---
observe mri_finding(symmetric_dentate_t2_flair_hyperintensity)

% --- neurologic course + signs ---
observe course(progressive_cognitive_decline)
observe exam_finding(pyramidal_signs_with_bilateral_extensor_plantars)
observe exam_finding(cerebellar_spastic_gait)

% --- the referral / attentional framing ---
observe presenting_request(adhd_type_inattention)
observe premorbid_trait(lifelong_inattentive)
observe test_result(positive_adult_inattention_screen)
observe test_result(full_scale_iq_borderline_mild)

% --- the considered (thyroid-autoimmune) workup + its failure ---
observe test_result(elevated_antithyroid_antibodies)
observe steroid_trial(no_benefit_then_worsening)
observe test_result(csf_bland_noninflammatory)

% NOT observed (open, decision-relevant): serum_cholestanol(...) and cyp27a1_testing(...)

% --- queries: each candidate diagnosis + the recommended next step ---
? diagnosis(cerebrotendinous_xanthomatosis)
? diagnosis(hashimoto_encephalopathy_sreat)
? diagnosis(adult_adhd)
? diagnosis(static_intellectual_disability)
? diagnosis(multiple_sclerosis)
